# MotionDot — Project Rules

Production batch GIF/MP4/WebP converter for TikTok, Instagram Reels, Threads, Coupang, and creators.

## Stack

Next.js (App Router) · TypeScript (strict) · Tailwind · Zustand · ffmpeg (`lib/ffmpeg`) · BullMQ · Redis · Remotion

## Folder architecture

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/` | Thin routes + `api/` only |
| `features/<name>/` | Isolated feature modules (`components/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `stores/`) |
| `components/` | **Shared** UI only — never duplicate in features |
| `lib/ffmpeg/` | **All** FFmpeg logic |
| `worker/` | **All** BullMQ workers + `processors/` |
| `presets/` | SNS specs as **JSON only** |
| `stores/` | Global Zustand |
| `types/` | Shared TS types |
| `temp/` | frames, gif, archive |
| `outputs/` | gif, mp4, webp finals |

## Pipelines

- **Upload**: `features/upload` → `POST /api/upload` → `temp/archive`
- **Preview**: `features/preview` → Remotion
- **Export**: `features/export` → `POST /api/jobs` → `outputs/`
- **Queue / progress**: `worker/` → Redis → `GET /api/jobs/progress`

## Rules

- Feature-based structure; isolated features
- No monolithic `page.tsx` — use `features/workspace`
- Strict TypeScript; `server-only` on fs/queue services
- Tailwind only
- Server barrels must not export `load-preset`, `upload-service`, `export-service` to client
- Import server helpers by full path: `@/features/presets/load-preset`

## Anti-patterns

- Duplicate components across features
- FFmpeg outside `lib/ffmpeg`
- Workers outside `worker/`
- Hardcoded preset dimensions when JSON exists
- Large page files

See `motiondot/ARCHITECTURE.md` for full map.
